Today is Sunday.
It was a very hot morning.
I could not bear the heat in the city.
I decided to escape from this heat.
I wanted to go to a coastal town in the south.
I quickly took my own bag.
Then I went outside and called an auto-rickshaw.
The auto driver was a very nice man.
"Where to?" he asked.
"To the Ernakulam railway station," I replied.
We reached the station at nine o'clock.
There was a huge crowd at the station.
I went to the ticket counter.
I bought a ticket to Alappuzha.
The ticket price was fifty rupees.
After that, I walked to the platform.
The platform was full of people.
I waited there for my train to arrive.
It was my first trip outside the city.
